At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

The Real Estate Locator&nbsp; is responsible for shaping and executing both the strategic vision and operational management of Flix’s infrastructure across the assigned Mexico region. It combines infrastructure development, stakeholder engagement, market analysis, and project coordination to support Flix’s expansion goals. The role is key to ensuring site accessibility, long-term planning, and alignment with public and private partners and new potential areas identified through field research.

About the Role

• Identify new potential markets and location opportunities aligned with Flix’s expansion strategy.

• Lead the sourcing, negotiation, and closing of contracts for new land or commercial space in pre-defined strategic areas or newly identified field locations.

• Oversee the validation of legal documentation to determine feasibility and define strategies for property accreditation and contract execution.

• Coordinate with property owners, developers, and legal teams to facilitate contract finalization.

• Administer and monitor multiple infrastructure and access projects simultaneously (10+), ensuring timely execution and cross-functional collaboration.

• Coordinate with Business Partners, Operations, and city officials to address and resolve infrastructure or permitting issues.

• Manage contract renewals and administrative processes with accuracy and legal alignment.

About You

• Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Urban Planning, Architecture, or a related field.

• Minimum of 4 years of experience in corporate real estate and commercial expansion, preferably in retail, hospitality, convenience stores, or similar sectors, with a focus on site selection, land negotiation, and commercial location scouting.

• In-depth knowledge of land documentation and legal processes (e.g., deeds, lease agreements, property taxes, water services).

• Willingness to travel is essential.

• Fluency in English is required.

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

What We Offer

• Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family.&nbsp;

• Work from (M)Anywhere : Depending on your role, work from another location for up to 60 days per year.&nbsp;

• Hybrid work model : We are an office-first company, but we offer flexibility to balance work and life.&nbsp;

• Wellbeing support : Access confidential 1:1 counselling, courses, and stress management for yourself and up to four family members.&nbsp;

• Learning &amp; Development : Take advantage of language classes, training courses, and expert-led sessions to grow your skills.&nbsp;

• Mentoring Program : Connect with experienced colleagues to gain insights and accelerate your career.&nbsp;

To view more local benefits specific to each office location, please check out this link:&nbsp; Locations - Flix Career

Why Join Flix?

At Flix, you’ll find teams that rally together to overcome challenges and spark creativity. We believe in ownership culture - giving you the freedom to take initiative, make an impact, and shape your own career path.
As we continue to expand across the globe, you can make a real difference in how we work.

If you’re ready to grow and lead your journey, Flix is the place for you!&nbsp;

